      "body": "## Motivation\n\nTwo NPU unit tests asserted behavior that no longer matches the current implementation, so they were guaranteed to fail (or never exercised):\n\n1. `test_fia_nz_without_mlapo_raises` in `test_npu_mla_preprocess.py` expected `is_fia_nz()` to raise when MLAPO is off. `is_fia_nz` now returns `SGLANG_USE_FIA_NZ` directly: FIA NZ is a cache-layout choice, not an MLAPO-only optimization, so models such as Kimi-K3 select it with MLAPO off. The old assertion always failed.\n\n2. `test_rejects_non_ue8m0_scale_format` in `test_npu_mxfp8_linear.py` expected a `ValueError` from `process_npu_arch35_mxfp8_linear_weights`, but that function never had such a guard: plain block-FP8 checkpoints carry arbitrary fp32 scales and are requantized through `_layout_npu_arch35_e4m3_weights`, so the test only ever reached `layer.weight.data` on an empty stub.\n\nThese two test fixes are split out of #46759 so that PR only carries test-case additions.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `test/registered/unit/npu/attention/test_npu_mla_preprocess.py`: rename `test_fia_nz_without_mlapo_raises` to `test_fia_nz_without_mlapo_returns_true` and assert `is_fia_nz()` returns `True` with `SGLANG_USE_FIA_NZ=1` and MLAPO unset.\n- `test/registered/unit/npu/quantization/test_npu_mxfp8_linear.py`: replace the never-raising reject test with `test_non_ue8m0_scale_format_uses_e4m3_requant_path`, asserting the e4m3 requant layout path is called once and the ue8m0 layout-only path is not.\n- Promote both files' `register_npu_ci` suite from `stage-a-unit-test-npu` (nightly-only) to `base-a-test-npu` so the fixed tests now run in the PR pipeline.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- No production code change; unit tests only (`stage-a-unit-test-npu` suite).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n- Not applicable; test-only change.\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41018325196](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41018325196)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41018325199](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41018325199)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41018325116](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41018325116)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
